        ns1:prov_source_passage "Robust evidence suggests that humans explore their environment using a combination of topological landmarks and coarse-grained path integration. This approach relies on identifiable environmental features (topological landmarks) in tandem with estimations of distance and direction (coarse-grained path integration) to construct cognitive maps of the surroundings. This cognitive map is believed to exhibit a hierarchical structure, allowing efficient planning when solving complex navigation tasks. Inspired by "^^xsd:string ;
        ns1:prov_source_section "abstract"^^xsd:string ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-07-25T02:04:48.720764+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
