        ns1:prov_source_passage "Extended finite state machines (EFSMs) model stateful systems with internal data variables and have numerous applications in software engineering. A major advantage of this type of model lies in its ability to model both the data flow and the data-dependent control behaviour. In the absence of such models, it is desirable to reverse-engineer them by observing the system's behaviour. However, existing approaches generally require the ability to reset the system during inference, or can only handle situations"^^xsd:string ;
