        ns1:prov_run_id "f198c4266b204f7393c0e15fcc1e18c4"^^xsd:string ;
        ns1:prov_source_passage "Measurement of a physical quantity such as light intensity is an integral part of many reconstruction and decision scenarios but can be costly in terms of acquisition time, invasion of or damage to the environment and storage. Data minimisation and compliance with data protection laws is also an important consideration. Where there are a range of measurements that can be made, some may be more informative and compliant with the overall measurement objective than others. We develop an active sequential infer"^^xsd:string ;
